[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:The Silent Village]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.43]Lesson 48 | 第48课
[00:02.45]The silent village | 沉默的村庄
[00:10.01]Why was the village silent? | 村庄为什么是沉默的？
[00:14.61]In this much-travelled world, there are still thousands of places which are inaccessible to tourists. | 在这个旅游频繁的世界上，仍然有成千上万个游客无法到达的地方。
[00:23.07]We always assume that villagers in remote places are friendly and hospitable. | 我们总是认为偏僻地方的村民友好而好客。
[00:29.74]But people who are cut off not only from foreign tourists, but even from their own countrymen can be hostile to travellers. | 但是，不仅与外国游客隔绝、甚至连与本国同胞也隔绝的人，却可能对旅行者怀有敌意。
[00:40.02]Visits to really remote villages are seldom enjoyable--as my wife and I discovered during a tour through the Balkans. | 到真正偏僻的村庄去访问很少是令人愉快的——我和妻子在巴尔干地区旅行时便发现了这一点。
[00:48.81]We had spent several days in a small town and visited a number of old churches in the vicinity. | 我们在一个小镇上待了几天，参观了附近的一些古老教堂。
[00:56.13]These attracted many visitors, for they were not only of great architectural interest, but contained a large number of beautifully preserved frescoes as well. | 这些教堂吸引了许多游客，因为它们不仅具有很大的建筑学上的价值，还保存着大量美丽的壁画。
[01:07.95]On the day before our departure, several bus loads of tourists descended on the town. | 我们离开的前一天，好几辆满载游客的公共汽车开到了镇上。
[01:14.50]This was more than we could bear, so we decided to spend our last day exploring the countryside. | 这使我们再也无法忍受，于是决定利用最后一天去乡村探险。
[01:22.86]Taking a path which led out of the town, we crossed a few fields until we came to a dense wood. | 我们走上一条出镇的小路，穿过几块田地，来到一片茂密的树林。
[01:30.38]We expected the path to end abruptly, but we found that it traced its way through the trees. | 我们以为小路会突然中断，却发现它蜿蜒穿行于树林之间。
[01:38.22]We tramped through the wood for over two hours until we arrived at a deep stream. | 我们在树林中跋涉了两个多小时，来到一条深深的溪流边。
[01:44.54]We could see that the path continued on the other side, but we had no idea how we could get across the stream. | 我们可以看到小路在溪流对岸延续，但不知道怎样才能过河。
[01:53.50]Suddenly my wife spotted a boat moored to the bank. | 突然，妻子发现岸边泊着一条小船。
[01:57.76]In it there was a boatman fast asleep. | 船里有个船夫正在酣睡。
[02:01.38]We gently woke him up and asked him to ferry us to the other side. | 我们轻轻地把他唤醒，请他把我们摆渡过河。
[02:06.67]Though he was reluctant to do so at first, we eventually persuaded him to take us. | 虽然起初他不愿意，但最后还是被我们说服了。
[02:13.23]The path led to a tiny village perched on the steep sides of a mountain. | 小路通向一座坐落在陡峭山坡上的小村庄。
[02:19.39]The place consisted of a straggling unmade road which was lined on either side by small houses. | 这个村子由一条蜿蜒的未经铺设的土路组成，路两旁排列着小房子。
[02:26.93]Even under a clear blue sky, the village looked forbidding, as all the houses were built of grey mud bricks. | 即使在蔚蓝的天空下，村子看上去也令人生畏，因为所有的房子都是用灰泥砖建造的。
[02:36.09]The village seemed deserted, | 村庄似乎被人遗弃了，
[02:38.49]the only sign of life being an ugly-looking black goat on a short length of rope tied to a tree in a field nearby. | 唯一的生命迹象是附近田地里一头用一小段绳子拴在树上的样子丑陋的黑山羊。
[02:49.12]Sitting down on a dilapidated wooden fence near the field, we opened a couple of tins of sardines and had a picnic lunch. | 我们在田边一段破烂的木栅栏上坐下来，打开两罐沙丁鱼，吃了顿野餐午餐。
[02:58.85]All at once, I noticed that my wife seemed to be filled with alarm. | 突然间，我注意到妻子似乎大惊失色。
[03:04.72]Looking up I saw that we were surrounded by children in rags who were looking at us silently as we ate. | 我抬头一看，只见我们被一群衣衫褴褛的孩子团团围住，他们默默地看着我们吃东西。
[03:13.30]We offered them food and spoke to them kindly, but they remained motionless. | 我们把食物递给他们，和善地同他们说话，可他们一动也不动。
[03:19.93]I concluded that they were simply shy of strangers. | 我断定他们只是怕生人。
[03:24.12]When we later walked down the main street of the village, we were followed by a silent procession of children. | 后来，我们沿村庄的主街行走时，一队孩子默默地跟在后面。
[03:32.46]The village which had seemed deserted, immediately came to life. | 刚才还似乎空无一人的村庄顿时活跃了起来。
[03:38.24]Faces appeared at windows. | 窗后露出了一张张面孔。
[03:40.40]Men in shirt sleeves stood outside their houses and glared at us. | 只穿衬衫的男人站在自家房外，瞪着眼看我们。
[03:45.78]Old women in black shawls peered at us from doorways. | 披黑头巾的老妇人从门廊里窥视我们。
[03:50.73]The most frightening thing of all was that not a sound could be heard. | 最令人恐惧的是四下里听不到一点声音。
[03:56.64]There was no doubt that we were unwelcome visitors. | 毫无疑问，我们是些不受欢迎的来访者。
[04:01.54]We needed no further warning. | 我们无需进一步的警告了。
[04:04.25]Turning back down the main street, | 转身沿主街往回走，
[04:06.60]we quickened our pace and made our way rapidly towards the stream where we hoped the boatman was waiting. | 我们加快脚步，迅速朝那条溪流走去，希望船夫正在那里等我们。
